{
 "issues": [
  {
   "analyst": "S1",
   "problem": "The shown final audit concatenates all carrier files, deduplicates, and computes the mean without filtering to scheduled departure dates in January and February 2025. It also treats Alaska's UTC date as an ordinary date and does not convert it to the origin airport's local scheduled date for month selection. Thus the reported value is not demonstrably restricted to the requested population."
  },
  {
   "analyst": "S2",
   "problem": "S2's method is generally appropriate, but its displayed standardized calculation computes the AS raw delay from UTC clock timestamps without explicitly handling a date rollover in the UTC date itself. The later threshold adjustment likely handles the intended post-midnight cases, but the code should explicitly verify that actual departures after midnight are represented as a next-day event. No concrete result error is established from this omission."
  },
  {
   "analyst": "S3",
   "problem": "The final calculation deduplicates and excludes cancellations but never filters records to January-February 2025. It calculates the mean over all unique records in the carrier files. It also reports the AS local-date boundary inspection but does not use local scheduled dates to filter the calculation. Therefore its 15.4 result is not supported as the requested Jan-Feb mean."
  }
 ],
 "disagreements": "All three report 15.4, but S1 and S3's shown final calculations do not apply the required January-February population filter. S2 explicitly filters to the requested months using the scheduled departure date and converts Alaska's UTC scheduled timestamp to the origin-local date. S2 also reports an unrounded mean of 15.4451, which rounds to 15.4. The common result may be coincidental if boundary records have little effect, but only S2's method is adequately aligned with the question.",
 "best": "S2",
 "correction": "Use the deduplicated, non-cancelled flights whose scheduled departure local date is in January or February 2025; for Alaska, convert the UTC scheduled timestamp to the origin airport's local date. Compute actual minus scheduled departure elapsed minutes, adding 1440 only for genuine next-day departures while retaining ordinary early departures as negative. The final JSON should remain {\"avg_delay_min\":15.4} if S2's stated 15.4451 mean is confirmed."
}
